<title>USA: DSI Toys plans larger IPO.</title>
<headline>DSI Toys plans larger IPO.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>DSI Toys Inc has increased the number of shares to be offered in its initial public offering to 3.0 million from 2.8 million said underwriter Tucker Anthony Inc.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to price between $9 and $11 per share in late May.</p>
<p>DSI Toys to trade on the Nasdaq under the symbol &quot;DSIT.&quot;</p>
<p>DSI Toys, based in Houston, designs, develops, markets and distributes value-priced toys and children's consumer electronics.</p>
